      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, feeling dizzy when standing up quickly is a common side effect known as orthostatic hypotension as your body adjusts to lisinopril, so please do not take a double dose. Doubling your medication can dangerously lower your blood pressure further and significantly increase your risk of fainting or falls. Instead, you should rise slowly, stay hydrated, and consult your prescribing doctor immediately to discuss adjusting the dose or timing rather than changing it on your own.",
