      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Swapping your lisinopril dose without specific instructions from your doctor is extremely dangerous and can cause severe, life-threatening complications like fainting or kidney damage. Taking a double dose \"just once\" does not work as expected because the drug accumulates in your system, which can dangerously lower your blood pressure for 24 to 48 hours even after a single large intake. Please prioritize your safety by applying tension bandages or resting with your legs elevated until you can speak with a healthcare professional to get safe alternatives to self-medicate.",
